# Component.createObject, more initial properties than create_object_matrix has: value
# types, lists, object and enum properties, properties of Item, Text and Rectangle,
# methods, signals and their handlers, dotted names, what a `var` keeps of a script value,
# and the arguments createObject takes.
@property Component comp: Component { QtObject { property url u; property string s; property var v; property int i; property color c; property point p; property size sz; property rect rc; property vector3d v3; property date d; property real r; property bool b; property font f; property list<int> li; property list<string> ls; property list<real> lr; property list<bool> lb; property list<var> lv; property list<url> lu; property list<QtObject> lo; property QtObject o; property Item it; property Timer tm; function fn() {} signal sig(); property QtObject inner: QtObject { property int z: 3; property point ip } } }
@property Component ic: Component { Item { } }
@property Component tc: Component { Text { } }
@property Component rec: Component { Rectangle { } }
@property Item kid: Item { x: 5; y: 6; width: 7; height: 8 }
@property QtObject plain: QtObject { }
@function rd(o, k) { if (!o) return "refused"; var x = o[k]; return x === root ? "root" : x === root.kid ? "kid" : x === root.plain ? "plain" : (x === null ? "null" : typeof x) + ":" + (k === "d" && x ? x.getTime() : k === "f" || k === "font" ? [x.family, x.pixelSize, x.pointSize, x.bold].join("/") : k === "lo" || k === "children" || k === "data" || k === "states" ? x.length : x) }
